<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter Paul Rubens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1577–1640</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter Paul Rubens was the leading painter of the Flemish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a>, born at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegen">Siegen</a> in Nassau, where his parents lived in exile. Trained in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antwerp">Antwerp</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, he ran a large workshop in Antwerp producing altarpieces, portraits and mythological scenes for the courts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and served as a diplomat for the Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, negotiating peace between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1629–1630.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-paul-rubens.jpg" alt="Peter Paul Rubens" width="320" height="439" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Paul Rubens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Self-portrait_-_RH.S.180_-_Rubenshuis_(after_restoration).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
